.TH tsort "" "Command"
.SH NAME
tsort \- topological sort
.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBtsort [\fIfile\fB]\fR
.SH DESCRIPTION
.HS
tsort -- topological sort
Usage:	tsort [ file ]
.HE
.B tsort
reads pairs of items from
.I file
(or the standard input, if no
.I file
is given) and prints, on the standard output, a sequence of all the
items such that each item comes before every item that must follow
it, according to the pairs given.
.PP
The input consists of pairs of items (words) separated by blanks,
tabs, or newlines.
A pair in which the two items are the same simply records that the
item is present in the input set.
Otherwise, a pair means that the first item must precede the second
in the output ordering.
.SH "SEE ALSO"
.B sort
.SH DIAGNOSTICS
.B tsort
reports and exits if its input holds an odd number of items, or if a
word is longer than 99 characters.
If the given ordering contains a cycle,
.B tsort
first dumps the items still involved in the cycle, in no particular
order, then reports `tsort: cycles' and exits with a nonzero status.
